{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552708-3e-infernals-would-you-rather","id":1552708,"title":"3E Infernals: Would you rather...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-28T17:50:49-07:00","id":1552708,"title":"3E Infernals: Would you rather...","content":"Aloha, doing a homebrew for Infernals for fun. With that I ask for any assistance.<br /> <br /> A) Would you rather have multiple charm trees per ability that expressed a given Yozi's input on that ability. This would easily generated a &quot;cute&quot; 666 charms.<br /> Example A) Archery. The Ebon Dragon has a tree that lets you shoot an arrow at one target and direct the arrow's shadow to another, while Malfeas has a tree that let's you blow a hole in a fortress wall, and Adorjan lets you shoot a swarm of arrows that you direct from round to round like a flock of birds until all the arrows are used up.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> B) A standardized set of baseline charms for each ability that have a ring of possible Yozi influences on that charm? This would cut down the number of &quot;Charms&quot; but possibly bloat the number of discrete elements. However it should make any given Crafter or Archer feel *<i>very</i>* unique.<br /> Example B) Archery. There's a charm that let's you produce a piece of ammunition. You can Invoke 1 or more of the Yozis when you use it to apply different effects. So invoking the Ebon Dragon makes the arrow a shadow allowing you to shoot it under a door or ambush with it in darkness, Malfeas causes it to deal massive amounts of Bashing damage to objects and structures, and Adorjan allows you to reroll all the dice that fail but direct the arrow to a different target in close or short range.<br /> \u200b<br /> In the case of A, capstone charms for abilities closely tied to a particular Yozi's wheelhouse grant a Devil-Body feature.<br /> In the case of B, as you acquire Invocations, you also acquire points to spend on mutations for your Devil-Body.<br /> Speaking of...<br /> <br /> I know a lot of folks didn't like the demon binding part of the Exaltation. I liked it, so would you rather...<br /> A) keep the 2e format<br /> OR<br /> B) have the demon be a cross between a smoke bomb and a cellphone to your Yozi masters. Here's what I'm thinking:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Devil-Body</b><br /> <br /> <b>Devil-Body is a Base Charm inherent to every Infernal. At its most basic it does 2 things.</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>It provides minor bonuses based on the 1st Circle Demon bound to the Infernal (like a Strength Boost for Blood Ape, maybe some kind of poison eating power for a Stomach Bottle Bug, etc. The bonuses manifest when the Infernal spends Essence to activate the Charm or automatically whenever they reach Bonfire+ Anima levels. As those Capstones or Invocations are acquired, the bonuses and traits it can grant improve but you spend Anima Banner to bring out more of them.</b></li> <li><b>As conceived, Devil Body is very Frieza-esque at this time, with a lot of \u201cthis isn\u2019t even my final form\u201d as you can repeatedly dump Anima Banner to scale it up at no cost</b></li> <li><b>At Essence 3, the Devil Body Charm is upgraded and whenever you reach Iconic Anima, you can dump your Anima down to Dim and spawn your 1st Circle Demon as a Pet which also benefits from those Capstone/Invocation Upgrades (so if you\u2019ve picked up a few by then, it might be on par with a Terrestrial Exalt on its own).</b></li> <li><b>At its most basic, this is a Panic Button/Get out of a Fight Free card. You dump your Anima and leave a powerful minion for any pursuers to fight. It\u2019s a badguy move that every Infernal can pull.</b></li> <li><b>I'm considering a thing where you can get extra points by dedicating them to the manifested demon, so they don't become part of your own Devil Body.</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Playing with a couple ideas like the XP you spend on those charms that earn Devil Body upgrades gets fed to the Demon to improve stats and skills, or using Wyld Mutations...</b></li> </ol></li> </ol>\u200b<br /> My current concept for the Infernal<br /> <br /> <b>Your power is your own, you are told. The only price the Yozis demand is greatness. </b><br /> <br /> <b>It isn\u2019t a lie, but the truth is more twisted. As Infernals ride wild through Creation, their excess fuels their legend. An Infernal does not win a battle, they annihilate their foes. They do not negotiate a compromise unless the scales of many are tipped in favor of their own interests. Anything less than absolute subjugation of an inferior is a sin. Followers, subordinates, even lovers must be exceptional. If they are not a peer, they are merely adornments.</b><br /> <br /> <b>And that is by design. Like all of the pewling mortality befouling Creation they are desperate for connection and recognition. Some Infernals will sally forth from the yawning maw of Malfeas and wreak havoc on those that slighted them, but more will charge forward seeking to regain a lost love or earn the recognition of a harsh mentor, and when they can't, they'll accept the fawning adoration of the multitudes as a substitute. They will seek to be heroes, yet never be content in that moniker. They must be the greatest, the most loved, and in short order they become numb to the soft accolades of the mundane. Soon enough the champions of Hell become desperate to insinuate themselves in Circles of other Celestial Exalts. </b><br /> <br /> <b>Their motives are always pure. They do want to make things better, exalt the world itself and be exalted within it. But the Great Curse lays heavy on their tainted souls and as their righteousness waxes, its power corrupts the hearts of those in whose eyes they shine.<br /> <br /> And that too is by design. Hell\u2019s Heroes unlock the doors behind which every mortal's shadowed heart beats.</b><br /> \u200b<br /> Their Role in the Reclamation<br /> <br /> The Infernal\u2019s Inner Demons (see Devil-Body) are automatically improved by the Infernal\u2019s acquisition of Devil-Body Charms or Invocations. The Yozi strategy is essentially to \u201ccross pollinate\u201d their own essences as these Infernals fuse normally inconsequential aspects of their being. Very quickly these Inner Demons will rival 2nd Circle Demons in power. Eventually, if made fat enough on their own pursuits of power, the Infernals will become a chain that fuses the Yozis into something just far enough from what they are to escape the oaths that bind them.<br /> <br /> Malfeas in particular championed this plan, expecting to become the head of this grotesquely wicked Voltron.<br /> <br /> Any input is appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28845-matt_c","name":"Matt_C","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T06:51:32-07:00","id":1552798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt_C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552708-3e-infernals-would-you-rather#post1552708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aloha, doing a homebrew for Infernals for fun. With that I ask for any assistance.<br /> <br /> A) Would you rather have multiple charm trees per ability that expressed a given Yozi's input on that ability. This would easily generated a &quot;cute&quot; 666 charms.<br /> Example A) Archery. The Ebon Dragon has a tree that lets you shoot an arrow at one target and direct the arrow's shadow to another, while Malfeas has a tree that let's you blow a hole in a fortress wall, and Adorjan lets you shoot a swarm of arrows that you direct from round to round like a flock of birds until all the arrows are used up.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> B) A standardized set of baseline charms for each ability that have a ring of possible Yozi influences on that charm? This would cut down the number of &quot;Charms&quot; but possibly bloat the number of discrete elements. However it should make any given Crafter or Archer feel *<i>very</i>* unique.<br /> Example B) Archery. There's a charm that let's you produce a piece of ammunition. You can Invoke 1 or more of the Yozis when you use it to apply different effects. So invoking the Ebon Dragon makes the arrow a shadow allowing you to shoot it under a door or ambush with it in darkness, Malfeas causes it to deal massive amounts of Bashing damage to objects and structures, and Adorjan allows you to reroll all the dice that fail but direct the arrow to a different target in close or short range.<br /> <br /> In the case of A, capstone charms for abilities closely tied to a particular Yozi's wheelhouse grant a Devil-Body feature.<br /> In the case of B, as you acquire Invocations, you also acquire points to spend on mutations for your Devil-Body.<br /> Speaking of...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather A, but only insofar as it's closer to what I think the Infernal design ought to be; Charms that are for the Exalted first and foremost, where the imagery of the Yozis is present insofar as it helps provide definition for what demonic Exalted applications of the Abilities look like, but not as overt as making every Ability consist of multiple parallel lines of Charms that are overtly modelled off of the Yozis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T17:18:35-07:00","id":1552816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552708-3e-infernals-would-you-rather?p=1552798#post1552798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would rather A, but only insofar as it's closer to what I think the Infernal design ought to be; Charms that are for the Exalted first and foremost, where the imagery of the Yozis is present insofar as it helps provide definition for what demonic Exalted applications of the Abilities look like, but not as overt as making every Ability consist of multiple parallel lines of Charms that are overtly modelled off of the Yozis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much for your reply, but I think my understanding of the Yozis nature of existence is making it hard for me to parse. Based on the 1st part of the sentence, I'd think you preferred option B.<br /> <br /> Example: according to my current understanding, &quot;Malfeas&quot; doesn't have melee charms, nor practice melee skills. It fought the Exalts and gods by being some kind of infinite context from which its Souls launched their campaign to suppress the uprising and again dominate Creation. Now, the &quot;Existence known as Malfeas&quot; is a big gross city monster thing. It exists and forms the context in which &quot;Hell&quot; manifests and is bound by oaths to continue to be that. I've read that there's some kind of Kaiju thing called a Jotun that it can operate as a kind of &quot;self&quot; but the destruction of that body has no real impact on Malfeas as a whole and I think its operation could begin and end with &quot;All the spirit charms its various souls know).<br /> <br /> Lieger has charms, but as a Demon, would use the rules for spirits. <br /> <br /> With all that in mind, I would think the main ingredient of all Infernal Charms would be a corrupted Solar exaltation. So at their core, the Charms would be similar and then colored by the Infernal through invocation of a specific Yozi. Note: Every charm would come with an initial Invocation they owe to their patron, but they'd be able to expand the application of those &quot;basic&quot; charms by adding the influence of additional Yozis, eventually creating effects that transcend their patrons.<br /> <br /> Or have I completely misread your intent and further confused the issue?<br /> <br /> Any further insight is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28845-matt_c","name":"Matt_C","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T21:16:29-07:00","id":1552821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt_C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552708-3e-infernals-would-you-rather?p=1552816#post1552816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you so much for your reply, but I think my understanding of the Yozis nature of existence is making it hard for me to parse. Based on the 1st part of the sentence, I'd think you preferred option B.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm not saying that individual Charms should have multiple configurations. I still think Yozi influences should be distributed among multiple Charms, with any given single Charm only really evincing one of them. Just that such Charms should not be segregated from one another by Yozi, and the Yozi influences are somewhat subtle. <br /> <br /> I'd look at the Abyssal Charms in comparison. Motifs drawn from the Deathlords are apparent, but Charms with different motifs can still follow after one another, and they're ultimately used to create an image of &quot;this is what the might of the Abyssal Exalted looks like&quot; rather than &quot;this is when the Abyssal is replicating a Heron Queen trick in Dodge&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the Yozis can serve as this inspiration if they are not just the sum total of their demons or exist in purely abstract state that can only be expressed literally through them. There is still a Malfeas, a will and identity that suffuses the hellish city and whose drives and foibles are part of the way it is, who exists apart from and presides over his souls (even if the actions and interactions of those souls feed back into that personality).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T17:51:20-07:00","id":1554905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt_C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552708-3e-infernals-would-you-rather#post1552708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aloha, doing a homebrew for Infernals for fun. With that I ask for any assistance.<br /> <br /> A) Would you rather have multiple charm trees per ability that expressed a given Yozi's input on that ability. This would easily generated a &quot;cute&quot; 666 charms.<br /> Example A) Archery. The Ebon Dragon has a tree that lets you shoot an arrow at one target and direct the arrow's shadow to another, while Malfeas has a tree that let's you blow a hole in a fortress wall, and Adorjan lets you shoot a swarm of arrows that you direct from round to round like a flock of birds until all the arrows are used up.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> B) A standardized set of baseline charms for each ability that have a ring of possible Yozi influences on that charm? This would cut down the number of &quot;Charms&quot; but possibly bloat the number of discrete elements. However it should make any given Crafter or Archer feel *<i>very</i>* unique.<br /> Example B) Archery. There's a charm that let's you produce a piece of ammunition. You can Invoke 1 or more of the Yozis when you use it to apply different effects. So invoking the Ebon Dragon makes the arrow a shadow allowing you to shoot it under a door or ambush with it in darkness, Malfeas causes it to deal massive amounts of Bashing damage to objects and structures, and Adorjan allows you to reroll all the dice that fail but direct the arrow to a different target in close or short range.<br /> <br /> In the case of A, capstone charms for abilities closely tied to a particular Yozi's wheelhouse grant a Devil-Body feature.<br /> In the case of B, as you acquire Invocations, you also acquire points to spend on mutations for your Devil-Body.<br /> Speaking of...<br /> <br /> I know a lot of folks didn't like the demon binding part of the Exaltation. I liked it, so would you rather...<br /> A) keep the 2e format<br /> OR<br /> B) have the demon be a cross between a smoke bomb and a cellphone to your Yozi masters. Here's what I'm thinking:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Devil-Body</b><br /> <br /> <b>Devil-Body is a Base Charm inherent to every Infernal. At its most basic it does 2 things.</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>It provides minor bonuses based on the 1st Circle Demon bound to the Infernal (like a Strength Boost for Blood Ape, maybe some kind of poison eating power for a Stomach Bottle Bug, etc. The bonuses manifest when the Infernal spends Essence to activate the Charm or automatically whenever they reach Bonfire+ Anima levels. As those Capstones or Invocations are acquired, the bonuses and traits it can grant improve but you spend Anima Banner to bring out more of them.</b></li> <li><b>As conceived, Devil Body is very Frieza-esque at this time, with a lot of \u201cthis isn\u2019t even my final form\u201d as you can repeatedly dump Anima Banner to scale it up at no cost</b></li> <li><b>At Essence 3, the Devil Body Charm is upgraded and whenever you reach Iconic Anima, you can dump your Anima down to Dim and spawn your 1st Circle Demon as a Pet which also benefits from those Capstone/Invocation Upgrades (so if you\u2019ve picked up a few by then, it might be on par with a Terrestrial Exalt on its own).</b></li> <li><b>At its most basic, this is a Panic Button/Get out of a Fight Free card. You dump your Anima and leave a powerful minion for any pursuers to fight. It\u2019s a badguy move that every Infernal can pull.</b></li> <li><b>I'm considering a thing where you can get extra points by dedicating them to the manifested demon, so they don't become part of your own Devil Body.</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Playing with a couple ideas like the XP you spend on those charms that earn Devil Body upgrades gets fed to the Demon to improve stats and skills, or using Wyld Mutations...</b></li> </ol></li> </ol><br /> My current concept for the Infernal<br /> <br /> <b>Your power is your own, you are told. The only price the Yozis demand is greatness. </b><br /> <br /> <b>It isn\u2019t a lie, but the truth is more twisted. As Infernals ride wild through Creation, their excess fuels their legend. An Infernal does not win a battle, they annihilate their foes. They do not negotiate a compromise unless the scales of many are tipped in favor of their own interests. Anything less than absolute subjugation of an inferior is a sin. Followers, subordinates, even lovers must be exceptional. If they are not a peer, they are merely adornments.</b><br /> <br /> <b>And that is by design. Like all of the pewling mortality befouling Creation they are desperate for connection and recognition. Some Infernals will sally forth from the yawning maw of Malfeas and wreak havoc on those that slighted them, but more will charge forward seeking to regain a lost love or earn the recognition of a harsh mentor, and when they can't, they'll accept the fawning adoration of the multitudes as a substitute. They will seek to be heroes, yet never be content in that moniker. They must be the greatest, the most loved, and in short order they become numb to the soft accolades of the mundane. Soon enough the champions of Hell become desperate to insinuate themselves in Circles of other Celestial Exalts. </b><br /> <br /> <b>Their motives are always pure. They do want to make things better, exalt the world itself and be exalted within it. But the Great Curse lays heavy on their tainted souls and as their righteousness waxes, its power corrupts the hearts of those in whose eyes they shine.<br /> <br /> And that too is by design. Hell\u2019s Heroes unlock the doors behind which every mortal's shadowed heart beats.</b><br /> \u200b<br /> Their Role in the Reclamation<br /> <br /> The Infernal\u2019s Inner Demons (see Devil-Body) are automatically improved by the Infernal\u2019s acquisition of Devil-Body Charms or Invocations. The Yozi strategy is essentially to \u201ccross pollinate\u201d their own essences as these Infernals fuse normally inconsequential aspects of their being. Very quickly these Inner Demons will rival 2nd Circle Demons in power. Eventually, if made fat enough on their own pursuits of power, the Infernals will become a chain that fuses the Yozis into something just far enough from what they are to escape the oaths that bind them.<br /> <br /> Malfeas in particular championed this plan, expecting to become the head of this grotesquely wicked Voltron.<br /> <br /> Any input is appreciated!</div> </div> </div> </div>My vote goes for A too, funnily enough for the exact opposite reasons stated above: Because I think it will be better for demonstrating the power of Infernals as conduits to the fallen titans whose legends take precedence over the Exaltation type they used to be.<br /> <br /> As for the demon binding thing? I'm mainly voting for B just because this is homebrew and I'm curious to see what you do with it. I've always found the Coadjutor less objectionable and more...underwhelming for what it is as the Infernal progresses, so by all means some sort of demonic utility belt sounds more interested.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just realised everything from the Devil-Body onwards was discussing something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","user":"Organ Boy","date":". 10-31-2025, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}